obligation.what_is_open:
The unresolved subclaim is the class-uniform estimate
\[
\inf_{\pi,\phi}\left\{\int\sum_i\operatorname{dist}_{\mathbb T}(T_i(z),\phi_i(z_i))^2d\lambda^n(z)\right\}^{1/2}
\le C\mathcal E^{(k+1)/(k+m+1)}
\]
for arbitrary bounded \(C^k\) transition diffeomorphisms after removal of coordinate means. Even in the primary case, the missing tangent estimate is weighted coercivity for every mean-zero divergence-free periodic \(C^2\) field, with weights vanishing on the Morse critical lines, followed by a nonlinear absorption of \(\det DT-1\) and the freely varying one-dimensional profiles. The frozen assumptions do not supply this inequality.

statements.statement:
For every fixed known \((k,m)\) and \(\alpha\in(0,1)\), the corrected inverted set obeys
\[
\inf_{\theta\in\mathcal M_{n,k,m}}
\Pr_\theta\{[h_\theta]\in\mathcal C_N(\alpha)\}
\ge1-\alpha-o(1).
\]
